WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.790
The air around you is
mostly nitrogen and oxygen.

2
00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:08.050
Those two gases can react with each
other to form nitrogen monoxide.

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.970
They're mixed together
in every breath you take.

4
00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:14.650
So why isn't the air turning
into nitrogen monoxide?

5
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.550
In this mission, you'll
meet dynamic equilibrium,

6
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:23.130
where the forward and backward reactions
never stop, even when nothing seems to change.

7
00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:25.370
You'll write equilibrium
constant expressions,

8
00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:28.810
and find out what the size of
K tells you about a reaction.

9
00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:34.350
Your mission: explain why the air
isn't turning into nitrogen monoxide.
